# Yuztoo website — DDD + file size (strict)

Stack: **Vite 6 + React 18, plain JavaScript (`.js` / `.jsx`, no TypeScript), no router.** Every
page is prerendered and listed in `src/routes.js`.

- **Firebase client**: do not import anything from `lib/firebase` (Firestore, Auth, Storage,
  Functions, App Check) outside `src/data/**` and `src/lib/**`. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` is
  configured as **error**. The same applies to raw `fetch` calls to our backend. Most pages ship
  zero Firebase — keep it that way.
- **Cloud Functions**: wrap every call in a named function in `src/data/**`
  (e.g. `src/data/submitLead.js`). Components and hooks call the wrapper, never `callFunction`.
- **Data shape**: always return `{ data, error }`, map raw documents to plain objects, never throw
  to the caller, read by ID, never scan a collection.
- **Content**: page copy, image `src` and `alt` belong in `src/site/<page>/<page>Content.js`, and
  SEO metadata in `src/site/<page>/<page>SeoData.js`. No user-facing string hard-coded in JSX.
- **Routes**: a new page means a new entry in `src/routes.js`, or it will not be prerendered and
  the SEO gate will fail.
- **No app or CRM code**: never import from the Flutter app (`lib/feature/**`) or the CRM.
  Duplicate shared constants in `src/siteConfig.js` with a comment naming the source of truth.
- **File length**: respect `max-lines` in `eslint.config.js` (data/lib/content/seo 800, pages 550,
  components/sections 450, rest 500). If a change would exceed the limit, split in the same change
  — never raise the ceiling.
- **Large hooks**: prefer composition (`useLeadFormState`, `useLeadSubmit`) over one monolith.

Full detail and the build pipeline: `docs/holy-books/DDD_HOLY_BOOK.md`.
